WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.548
Am I afraid of being buried
alive?

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.218
Yeah, I don’t think I’d love it.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:13.597
I’d prefer to be buried alive
than to burn to death in a fire.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:17.309
I would hate to be buried alive,
that’s why I’m going to get
cremated.

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:20.646
Ironically, I’d be, I’d still be
burned but that’s after I’ve...

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.731
Yeah, you wouldn’t be dead
before you’re burnt to death.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:23.774
Yeah, I think that’s...

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.109
Uh, just to check in, how much
of this is usable?

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.570
(Laughing)

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:34.451
The first time I was like, I
really, really love doing these
scenes with you

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:38.830
and I want to do lots of more
scenes with you, was in episode
four at the gala.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:39.831
I’m switching tables.

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:41.875
No, no, no, no, no, hey. Come on
back here.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.504
Phil Dunster:
I loved watching you do that
because, you can see the depth,

00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:48.423
Phil Dunster:
and like all the memories and
like the years of frustration and pain

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:51.593
but also like the ambition that
you had and the optimism that you
used to have

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:57.015
and I was like this is, I love
working with somebody who can do
that.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:58.475
That’s the nicest thing you’ve
ever said.

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.435
I loved you from day one.

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:01.979
And I’m not ashamed to say it.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:05.524
And I remember in the first read
through, I was like, you’re very
good you’re very good

00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:13.407
because I always like an actor
who isn’t scared of the negative
aspects

00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:17.452
of their character. That doesn’t
try to just charm them away, you
know what I mean?

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:18.078
Yeah.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:23.208
If you could inhabit one of your
co-star's bodies for a day, who
would it be?

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.835
Yours. How ‘bout you? Whose...

00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:25.877
Whose body would I inhabit if I
could?

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:27.337
Yeah, whose body would you
inhabit?

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:30.173
What you’re asking me, is, will
you objectify a member of the
cast?

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:31.591
And I absolutely would.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.050
Phil Dunster:
Yeah.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.885
But not, not in public.

00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:37.597
There’s a bit when we head-butt
each other.

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:40.183
What’d ya do that for!?

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:41.643
So I could do this!

00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:44.980
Yeah, and we left a scar on it.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:45.314
Phil Dunster:
Yeah.

00:01:45.314 --> 00:01:47.733
-Still have it to this day
‘cause we really went for it. 
- Yeah. Mine's internal.

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:50.485
Mine’s here. But, do you know
what, Brett?

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:52.362
I think it’s one of those, it’s,
it’s one of those things

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.948
that just happened over time and
then one day I woke up 

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.242
and I thought, gosh, I thought,
heavens.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:58.660
He's in my bed again.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.330
He's in my heart.

00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:02.205
Yeah.

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.915
-And metaphorically in my bed.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:04.833
And wherever I go.

00:02:07.294 --> 00:02:10.047
I can’t get through a scene with
you despite loving you and all
that 

00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:12.841
and I love doing scenes with
you. You make me laugh in every
scene

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:16.011
in a really bad way, like, like
we’re in church.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.056
It's like someone’s farted and
you’re not allowed to laugh.

00:02:19.056 --> 00:02:21.266
And I always wondered why it is,
and I think it’s

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.477
because we often have scenes
where we’re really close.

00:02:23.477 --> 00:02:24.311
We do, yeah!

00:02:24.311 --> 00:02:26.104
Brett Goldstein:
Our faces are always very close
to each other.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:26.980
Phil Dunster:
Much proximity.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:27.856
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:30.692
Phil Dunster:
Do you remember?

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:31.318
Brett Goldstein:
Yeah.

00:02:31.526 --> 00:02:32.361
Season two?

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:32.986
Yeah, I remember.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.447
Phil Dunster:
There’s a scene where you hug
me.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.412
Brett Goldstein:
That is the only scene I have
not laughed in because it was very moving

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:43.497
Brett Goldstein:
and you were so brilliant.

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:46.208
That was like a really special,
we were all in it.

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.376
We were really in that scene,
all of us.

00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:47.959
Phil Dunster:
Yeah.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.295
You also had to do that with a
massive audience,

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:54.591
like it wasn’t just the crew, it
was like everyone in the cast
was in that scene

00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.551
Brett Goldstein:
and it was a long day, it was
all day doing that

00:02:57.386 --> 00:03:00.347
and you’re right, everyone is
usually distracted

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:04.935
but I think you also held
everyone. It was really amazing.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:05.894
Thanks, man.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.521
You’re a good boy.

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:10.565
Who do you think on the show
would be easiest to deep fake?

00:03:10.982 --> 00:03:14.111
I think it’s probably me
because I do the least amount of
movement.

00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:15.821
That is true. Yeah.

00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:19.282
So you just, you can just put
like my face on a stick and just
walk it around.

00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:20.867
You’d probably be fine.

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:27.332
Phil Dunster:
In my mind you had a persona of,
you are one of the leads in this show, 

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:29.960
Phil Dunster:
you’ve got a huge body of work
behind you,

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.504
but you are just as much of an
idiot as I am. Because you...

00:03:32.504 --> 00:03:33.422
Brett Goldstein:
Yeah, yeah.
I remember you thinking...

00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:34.673
I saw your eyes light up.

00:03:34.673 --> 00:03:38.385
...you seem like really highbrow
and so clever and then you’d be
like beep boop beep.

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:39.010
Phil Dunster:
Yeah.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.679
Brett Goldstein:
I’d be laughing and you’d be
like, oh, this is easy.

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:43.974
One of the first jokes that I
think we had was the...

00:03:43.974 --> 00:03:44.516
Brett Goldstein:
Oh, yeah.

00:03:44.516 --> 00:03:47.894
We’d start doing this because we
didn’t want people to hear us
doing these stupid voices.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:48.603
Brett Goldstein:
Yeah.

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:49.980
And making silly noises.

00:03:50.105 --> 00:03:50.939
Brett Goldstein:
And then sound came in 

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:52.357
Phil Dunster:
Because we’re just silly, aren’t
we? We’re just silly.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:52.983
Brett Goldstein:
Silly boys.

00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:54.484
But, seriously, I love you.

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:55.068
I love you.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.820
I think you’re amazing.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.279
I think you’re amazing.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:02.242
At this, at writing it, also
telling me which bits are,
like how to make it funny.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.535
Cause I genuinely, I don’t know,
you know, 

00:04:03.535 --> 00:04:06.997
there’s times where I have to be
like, how do I say this when
it’s funny.

00:04:06.997 --> 00:04:09.332
And I love you for teaching me
that

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:13.086
and thank you also for
having a really nicely sculpted
body.

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:20.218
Phil, you’re a fantastic actor.

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:21.970
Truly a brilliant actor, you can
do anything.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.181
You can do anything. You can do
all the voices.

00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:25.974
You can sing, you can dance.

00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:27.726
You’ve taught me a dance move or
two.

00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:28.518
I have.

00:04:28.518 --> 00:04:32.147
You’re the funniest person I
know, probably.

00:04:32.147 --> 00:04:32.606
Wow.

00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:33.523
Top five.

00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:35.025
Phil Dunster:
Top five.

00:04:35.025 --> 00:04:36.359
I know a lot of funny people,
I’m in comedy.

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:37.110
You do, you’re a comedian.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:37.944
I know a lot of funny people.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.155
-I’m, listen, I’m thrilled with
top five.
-I’m putting you top five.

00:04:40.155 --> 00:04:40.864
Yeah.

00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:43.617
Should we sign off with our
dance move?

00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:44.326
No.

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:46.870
Do you wanna? You don’t wanna. 

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.706
-We can do the face that you
taught, the dance face.
-Okay

00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:55.545
Commit. Commit.

00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:01.134
That's what they wanna see.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.220
Okay, thank you very much.

